data.content:
Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)**. In MSTest v4, `TestMethodAttribute`'s constructor gained `[CallerFilePath]` and `[CallerLineNumber]` parameters. Your custom subclass must propagate these, and `[TestMethod("name")]` must use `DisplayName =`.

Here's the fix:

```csharp
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;
using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;

namespace MyApp.Tests;

public class CategorizedTestMethodAttribute : TestMethodAttribute
{
    public string Category { get; }

    public CategorizedTestMethodAttribute(
        string category,
        [CallerFilePath] string callerFilePath = "",
        [CallerLineNumber] int callerLineNumber = -1)
        : base(callerFilePath, callerLineNumber)
    {
        Category = category;
    }
}
```

And for the `[TestMethod("My custom display name")]` usage, change to:

```csharp
[TestMethod(DisplayName = "My custom display name")]
```

